      "section": "2. General Safety Precautions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.22,
        "t": 742.45466,
        "r": 286.348482,
        "b": 648.5632409281769
      },
      "content": "Do not pull out or modify the instruments or electric circuits installed for a safety such  as  the stroke  limit  dog  of  feed  system,  the limit  switch,  the  interlock  limit  switch, and etc.",
      "section_id": "sec_2",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 1,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_2",
          "title": "2. General Safety Precautions"
        }
      ],
      "page": 21,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0154",
      "reading_order": 180,
      "section": "2. General Safety Precautions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.22,
        "t": 640.4550680000001,
        "r": 286.373532,
        "b": 597.563444928177
      },
      "content": "Check  the  belt  for  tension.  Make  it sure that your hands of fingers are not hold between the belt and the pulley.",
      "section_id": "sec_2",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 1,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_2",
          "title": "2. General Safety Precautions"
        }
      ],
      "page": 21,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0155",
      "reading_order": 181,
      "section": "2. General Safety Precautions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.22,
        "t": 572.4152600000001,
        "r": 527.3425080000006,
        "b": 546.563648928177
      },
      "content": "Always clamp the workpiece or the tool exactly. For the cutting depth and feederate, begin form the minimum level.",
      "section_id": "sec_2",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 1,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_2",
          "title": "2. General Safety Precautions"
        }
      ],
      "page": 21,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0156",
      "reading_order": 182,
      "section": "2. General Safety Precautions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.21999999999994,
        "t": 385.4560880000002,
        "r": 527.1912059999999,
        "b": 359.54435692817697
      },
      "content": "When the machine rotated at a high speed, the clamping force of chuck will be decreased rapidly. Be careful to set up the pressure of chuck and cylinder.",
      "section_id": "sec_2",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 1,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_2",
          "title": "2. General Safety Precautions"
        }
      ],
      "page": 21,
      "chunk_hint": "continue",
      "semantic_role": "description",
      "source": "pdf_text"
    },
    {
      "type": "list_item",
      "id": "txt_0157",
      "reading_order": 183,
      "section": "2. General Safety Precautions",
      "bbox": {
        "l": 92.21899799999991,
        "t": 351.4361840000002,
        "r": 527.2002239999996,
        "b": 308.5445609281769
      },
      "content": "When  chucking  and  centering  the  center  workpiece,  take  care  of  its  weight,  the  hole  of center, configuration, and thrust of center. If centering and loading through a small hole, the lead-edge of center may be broken and the workpiece sprung out.",
      "section_id": "sec_2",
      "parent_section_id": null,
      "section_level": 1,
      "section_path": [
        {
          "id": "sec_2",
          "title": "2. General Safety Precautions"
        }
      ],
